  have serious shoe Envy once they see  them when you first see Wednesday she's  in her iconic white collared black dress  outfit but then as The Show Goes On Her  Style evolves they always wanted her to  stand out from the crowd in some way  number eight one of the most important  factors of the show's look Romania is  not a location that you'll often see in  the media so capturing that grandiose  Eastern European Vibe was a huge  inspiration for both the cast and crew I  did send a photograph of my myself in my  office to my agent and said is this what  your office looks like number nine there  are a lot of subtleties to Jenna  Ortega's performance Wednesday's  somebody that I always was compared to  my entire life though the show Runners  found her to be a perfect fit for the  character she was nervous to portray her  because she wanted so badly to do the  character Justice I went to fencing  lessons twice a week  I went to cello lessons twice a week  everywhere she went she would walk like  Wednesday she thought people would think  she was insane with how much she was  putting into nailing down the character  I wanted her to be specific and certain  and assertive number 10. Tim Burton had  a very specific vision for Wednesday  according to Jenna he was one of the  most detail-oriented directors she'd  ever worked with the thing that makes  Tim a great visual director is that he  has an amazing sense of color and style  he liked to have a say in how every shot  was framed and even the type of lens  used on the camera because he kind of  liked when they were wide and a bit  disoriented he designed and brought to  life every single character with  sketches goth comes to him very  naturally and Tim designed what the  Monster looks like in the show number 11  what kind of show would this be without  the appearance of the original Wednesday  Addams Christina Ricci joins the cast as  Marilyn Thornhill a teacher at Nevermore  Academy it is scary it's a lot of  pressure and you you want to do justice  to someone like her you would think that  Jenna and Christina would be having some  pretty intense conversations about the  character they've both portrayed right  the strange thing is we never talked  about her being Wednesday once there was  only one time on the last day of  shooting that Jenna made a reference to  Christina's version of Wednesday they  both had an understanding and an  acceptance that their versions were  going to be different number 12. did you  know Jenna always wanted to star in a  silent film it is a hard thing to play  with an expressionless character the  origin of most of Wednesday's mannerisms  and movements came from the idea of it  being shot like a silent film I felt  like that really encouraged mannerisms  or kind of balance the aspects of  surrealism and realism in the film Tim  Burton really connected with the idea as  well given the fact that the way Jenna  conveyed emotion most of the time was  silently through her Expressions because  they can be very theatrical and dramatic  and intense and that is what Adam's  family is number 13 Wednesday was  originally a Latina character in The  Addams Family Comics one of the most  important parts of this role for Jenna  Ortega was getting to represent  Wednesday as a Latina because it has  never been done before anytime that I  have an opportunity to represent my  community I want that to be seen another  way Tim Burton wanted to make this known  was by exemplifying the fact that the  Addams Family participates in Dia de los  Muertos I was just in the living room  more seating for a year-long Dia de los  Muertos number 14. the entire town was  built from the ground up coupled with  the extraordinary setting of Romania the  set of the show was like a character in  itself Gwendolyn Christie talks about  her experience at New York Comic-Con  what I loved was that we filmed in  Romania so you have Landscapes that had  not been seen before it's almost like  looking at things with quite a fresh  pair of eyes on an epic scale and much  of what you see is real this team really  went all out they built a town and used  locations and there's an awful lot of  authenticity to bring that very specific  culture to life number 15 can you  imagine getting an email from Tim Burton  Jenna was busy filming the horror movie  X as conversations about Wednesdays  started to come up at Netflix Tim Burton  was the one who thought about her for  the role as he was a fan of her work so  he sent her an email asking if they  could meet I kind of felt like I was  being pranked or something naturally  everyone fell in love with her  performance right away because I'm very  dry and I don't think people can tell  when I'm being serious or when I'm being  sarcastic with Tim Burton behind the  show along with his incredible  hand-picked cast and crew Wednesday is  an iconic piece of media in the making  with your favorite behind the scenes  moment
 

